.TH GIT-OPEN 1 "2026-11-10" "git-open" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-open \- open a git repository, file, or commit in the browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-open
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path | commit ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-open
opens the current repository in the web browser. With an argument, it opens
that file, folder, or commit instead. Providers are matched by the host of the
remote URL.
.PP
If the argument is missing, outside the repository, or not found, the
repository root is opened.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat every following argument as a path, even if it begins with a dash.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I path
A file or folder in the repository. A trailing
.I :line
or
.I :start\-end
opens that line or range of lines of a file.
.TP
.I commit
A commit hash of 7 to 64 hexadecimal characters.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Providers other than github.com, gitlab.com, bitbucket.org and codeberg.org
are added with git config. Local repository config takes precedence over global.
.TP
.B open.<url>.commitprefix
Path segment between the repository and a commit hash. Required.
.TP
.B open.<url>.pathprefix
Path segment between the repository and a ref. Required.
.TP
.B open.<url>.lineformat
Line anchor template where
.B %l
is a line number. At most two
.B %l
may be given, for the start and end lines. Optional.
.PP
.RS
.EX
git config \-\-global open.https://git.example.com.commitprefix commit
git config \-\-global open.https://git.example.com.pathprefix tree
git config \-\-global open.https://git.example.com.lineformat "L%l\-L%l"
.EE
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ git open
$ git open main.go
$ git open main.go:42\-50
$ git open 7605d91
$ git \-C ~/src/my\-repo open
$ git open \-\- \-odd\-file\-name
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
